Task: Build the hospital-year financial panel (+ Medicaid expansion table) — Phase 1.

Summary: New hospital (CCN) x year panel from NASHP HCT replaces the demand-side
county-summed Hosp_BadDebt_PerCapita for the supply-side analysis. Preserves
provider heterogeneity that county aggregation destroys.

Created:
 - Code/process_hospital_panel.R: build_hospital_panel() + pure helpers
   (pad_fips, classify_ownership, derive_uncomp, derive_safetynet). Reads the
   Downloadable sheet, derives outcomes/moderators, CPI-deflates to $2023, maps
   Zip->county (one-to-one crosswalk; modal county; 98.4% match), attaches county
   shocks+lags from county_level_master.csv (97.7%). Heavy build guarded by
   sys.nframe()==0 so tests can source helpers without rebuilding.
 - Code/medicaid_expansion.R: KFF ACA-expansion adoption years -> medicaid_expanded().
 - Code/tests/test_hospital_panel.R: 6 unit + 9 integration tests, all pass.

Output (gitignored): Data/intermediate_hospital_panel.rds — 59,896 hospital-years,
5,119 hospitals, 2011-2023.

Why: provider heterogeneity (ownership/safety-net/system/payer mix) is a hospital
attribute; the supply-side (proposal Ch.2) analysis must run at hospital-year.

Units verified: margins/payer-mix/%NPR are proportions; dollars raw -> $2023.
